 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the alienation of certain parklands in the village of\nTarrytown, in the town of Greenburgh, in the county of Westchester",
    "basePrintNo": "S5120",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5120-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5120\n\nSPONSOR: STEWART-COUSINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act authorizing the alienation of certain parklands\nin the village of Tarrytown, in the town of Greenburgh, in the county of\nWestchester\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA:\n\nTo authorize the Village of Tarrytown to discontinue the use of certain\nland presently dedicated for parkland to complete a transfer of land\npreviously agreed to by the Village and to make an undersized and irreg-\nularly shaped parcel more zoning compliant.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the village of Tarrytown to discontinue\nas parklands and alienate certain lands for completing a transfer of\nland previously agreed to by the village and to make an undersized and\nirregularly shaped parcel more zoning compliant.\n\nSection 2 provides that the authorization provided in section one of the\nact will only be effective on the condition that the village of Tarry-\ntown dedicate the lands described in section 4 as parkland; provided\nthat the village has never used such lands for public open space\npurposes.\n\nSection 3 provides a legal description of the parklands to be discontin-\nued.\n\nSection 4 describes the replacement land to be acquired and dedicated by\nthe village of Tarrytown as parkland.\n\nSection 5 provides that in the event the land acquired and dedicated as\nparkland is not equal to or greater than the fair market value of the\nparklands to be alienated, the village of Tarrytown shall acquire and\ndedicate additional land for parkland and/or cause funds to be made\navailable for capital improvements to its existing park and recreational\nfacilities, as necessary, to equal such difference in fair market value.\n\nSection 6 provides that if the village of Tarrytown received any funding\nsupport or assistance from the federal government for the purchase,\nmaintenance or improvement of the parklands to be alienated, the discon-\ntinuance and alienation of the parkland shall not occur until the\nvillage of Tarrytown has complied with any federal requirements pertain-\ning to the lands including compliance with any conditions imposed by the\nsecretary of the interior.\n\nSection 7 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2011 the Village of Tarrytown purchased 11.38 acres of land that was\npart of a subdivision that created both open space parcels and parcels\nto be developed. As part of the subdivision planning the Village Plan-\nning Board agreed to sell a small parcel of land (approximately 3,301\nsq. ft.) to a neighboring property owner in order make their property\nmore zoning compliant. During the course of the review process which\n\ntook several years, this agreed to transfer of land was inadvertently\noverlooked.\n\nThis legislation will authorize the Village of Tarrytown to discontinue\nthe use of a small piece of parkland to complete a transfer previously\nagreed to while ensuring that the Village receives parkland or capital\nimprovements to current parkland and recreational facilities of equal or\ngreater value.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State. Undetermined for the local government.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
